  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes the maximum and minimum outcomes of the lotteries. The individual explicitly considers the maximum outcome (higher possible gain), which aligns with the decision reason. The decision reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome—which is Lottery B (4000 > 3000)—and the individual appears to favor this same aspect. Although the individual also mentions the small difference in probability, this does not contradict the use of the outcome-based reason; rather, it supplements it by contextualizing the trade-off. However, the core justification—'higher possible gain'—matches the primary criterion of the decision reason. The minimum outcomes are identical (0 Euros), so the tie-breaking rule of the reason is not needed. The individual’s focus on the superior maximum outcome strongly suggests use of this reason, even if probability is mentioned as a secondary consideration. Therefore, the decision reason was likely used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

{
